WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:06.400
Hallå! Welcome to Ikea, where our motto is:
You get what you pay for, and sometimes, a

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.180
little less! You may think the greatest frustration
you’ll receive from heading down to your

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:16.410
local Ikea warehouse is spending a few hours
walking around the labyrinthine showroom,

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.829
or maybe arguing with your partner in broken
Swedish about the correct way to put together

00:00:20.829 --> 00:00:25.710
a Björksnäs. Or perhaps even needing to
slide a piece of cardboard under the front-left

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.389
corner of your Pax wardrobe cause otherwise
it’ll wobble.

00:00:29.389 --> 00:00:35.309
But these are nothing compared to you getting
trapped inside of SCP-3008, also known as

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:40.570
the Infinite Ikea. Not only can you spend
so long in this eternal flat-pack purgatory

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:46.300
that your bones may turn to dust on the showfloor,
but the murderous Staff - those are the malformed,

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:52.390
faceless weirdos in Ikea uniforms - will hunt
you down and beat you to death for not leaving.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:57.200
And believe us, leaving is a whole lot harder
than you’d like to think. That’s why we

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:03.140
put the question to you: How would you survive,
or even escape, “SCP-3008 - The Infinite

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:08.320
Ikea?” and these are your best and most
interesting answers...

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.000
Connor Nolan said, “With limitless refilling
food, and a vast expanse of Ikea tool kits

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.020
and construction materials, the endless IKEA
sounds like a pretty alright place to be stuck,

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.390
all things considered.”

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:24.119
We love your positive attitude, Connor. Sometimes,
having a nice outlook on life can make any

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:29.329
situation - even being stranded in a dimension
full of affordable Swedish furniture - just

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:33.689
that little bit nicer. However, if you want
to survive, you’re also going to need to

00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:38.299
be realistic. During the day, yes, the worst
you’ll have to deal with is getting lost,

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:42.780
the risk of not having food, and the existential
horror of knowing you may draw your last breath

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.630
inside an Ikea.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:49.390
But at night, the Staff will actively hunt
and try to kill you, and if you’re not prepared,

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:54.820
believe us, they will. So, by all means, keep
your optimism, but don’t allow that sunny

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:59.640
attitude to allow you to drop your guard - or
the next set of meatballs might be made out

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.780
of you.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.359
Purple Panda said, “I would simply hide
in one of the cabinets in the kitchen aisle

00:02:04.359 --> 00:02:08.740
for the night, then come out during the day
for food, and return back to my tiny lodge,

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:13.080
and then rinse and repeat until I die of old
age. And for extra protection, I'd duct tape

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.910
the inside of the cabinet door at night. It
wouldn't be much different from my current

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:17.910
life...”

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:21.880
Now that’s a little more like it. It’s
not a bad idea to keep things simple while

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:27.200
you’re trapped inside SCP-3008, and making
a cabinet your home is a good way to potentially

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.140
avoid the wrath of the Staff. However, getting
a little bit of Connor’s more hopeful mentality

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:37.090
may also help. After all, why resign yourself
to dying inside the Ikea when you can keep

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:42.200
the fires of hope alive - like the kind of
flames produced by a lovely Sinnlig scented

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.360
candle, available at Ikea for a dollar forty-nine.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.340
Dirt said, “Dig a hole. Just dig a giant
tunnel system underground and put rugs over

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:54.280
the entrances. Have tunnels going to sources
of food, water, etc. Staff won’t find you

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.750
if you cover your entrances. You might say,
however, “where do we get digging tools?”

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:02.490
The garden section or just make them. This
would be a long project so you would most

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.230
likely have to stay in a small base until
you dig enough.”

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:10.270
This idea is certainly ambitious. Your biggest
problem is probably that the only digging

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:15.800
equipment available in Ikea is the Gräsmarö,
a $4.99 set of three gardening tools including

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:20.800
a tiny hand-shovel. Given that the actual
layout of the Ikea appears unpredictable and

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.680
ever-expanding, it would also be incredibly
difficult to properly plan and create tunnels

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.870
- even if you had decades to do it. Though
of course, maybe you’re an expert tunneler,

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.900
and if that’s the case, we apologize sincerely
for besmirching your honor.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.940
Llama Fan said, “I would make a wall of
toilets and live off of crayons.”

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.970
We have good news and bad news. The good news
is that Ikea stocks the Måla 12-piece crayon

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:48.510
set, giving you a delicious variety of colors
to try while trapped in the infinite Ikea.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:53.180
The bad news is that these crayons have pretty
much no nutritional value, so your flushing

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:57.660
fortress may actually become a porcelain prison
as your body and mind slowly give out from

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.500
a lack of sustenance.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.850
Getting bludgeoned to death by the Staff inside
of your toilet tower would probably be a mercy

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:04.850
in the end.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:08.920
G W said, “I would honestly stay if I got
stuck there, with things like "when day breaks"

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:13.040
over the horizon. Build a home on the steel
supports overhead using a pull up ladder to

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.750
get up and down and live as comfortably as
possible.”

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:21.930
This is certainly a valid point. A number
of horrific XK-Class End of the World Scenarios,

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:27.520
like SCP-001, the dreaded “When Day Breaks”
event, wouldn’t actually affect the inside

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:33.070
of the infinite Ikea - seeing as its lights
function as a kind of internal sun. And if

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:37.330
it’s high enough above sea level, you wouldn’t
have to worry much about climate change, either.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:42.180
The Staff trying to beat you to death every
night may put a damper on things, though...

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.560
Sanic Hedgehog said, “I don't think "The
Staff" are faster than the speed of sound.”

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.650
That’s true, Sanic, but there are also no
chilli dogs inside the Infinite Ikea, and

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:52.969
that’s no good.

00:04:52.969 --> 00:04:56.669
Kai Wilkey said, “When it comes to day time
I’d search for other survivors that are

00:04:56.669 --> 00:05:00.830
inside with me, I would work with them to
build a civilization and live together. as

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:04.509
it gets close to night I’d search for food
and supplies to keep us alive through the

00:05:04.509 --> 00:05:08.900
night. When it becomes morning I’d clean
up the bodies and search for more survivors.”

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:13.800
This is one of the most tried and true methods
of long-term survival in the Infinite Ikea.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:19.240
However, as you’ll find with almost everything
in life, it’s easier said than done. Even

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:24.139
some of the largest settlements inside 3008
have been destroyed by careless decisions.

00:05:24.139 --> 00:05:29.389
After all your months and years of hard work
building up fortifications, gathering supplies,

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:33.419
creating a new form of entertainment where
you turn Tvålsjön toilet brushes into puppets

00:05:33.419 --> 00:05:38.629
that perform inside of a cardboard box, all
of that effort can be lost in a split second

00:05:38.629 --> 00:05:43.460
when one person forgets to lock the Karlby
countertop fence and Staff members come flooding

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.460
in.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.710
Hazel said, “If they had a Wi-Fi connection
and I had my phone, food, and a shower I would

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:51.770
be 100% fine. And maybe a TV?”

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:57.800
Good news! Ikea has wifi and food. Bad news:
Unless you can, by some act of pure luck,

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:02.190
find the staff quarters, there’s unlikely
to be a shower in the building. Not a working

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:07.449
one at least. The appliances in the bathroom
section are not operational and frankly, they

00:06:07.449 --> 00:06:11.919
should warn you of that to avoid embarrassing
situations. But enough about why we’re banned

00:06:11.919 --> 00:06:17.279
from the local Ikea, because there’s more
bad news: There are no TVs in Ikea, though

00:06:17.279 --> 00:06:21.669
you can get yourself a classy and tasteful
Brimnes TV stand, and simply imagine that

00:06:21.669 --> 00:06:27.099
the fake TV sitting on it is real. Or there’s
always the Tvålsjön toilet brush puppets…

00:06:27.099 --> 00:06:31.659
MobRecon said, “I would dress up as an Ikea
employee, and when the staff try to attack

00:06:31.659 --> 00:06:33.529
me I'd just claim to work there.”

00:06:33.529 --> 00:06:38.190
We think your heart is in the right place,
but considering the Staff within 3008 don’t

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:41.999
look human at all, you’ll probably need
to go a little more extreme to convince them

00:06:41.999 --> 00:06:44.810
that you’re one of them. Like Greyson K.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:50.029
Greyson K said, “I remember from one video
about SCP-3008 that the Staff are completely

00:06:50.029 --> 00:06:54.009
empty, they have no organs at all, so what
someone could do is just wear the hollowed-out

00:06:54.009 --> 00:06:57.400
Staff as a costume to move among other staff
at night.”

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:02.630
See, that’s dedication to the performance.
True, frightening dedication. Seeing that

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:07.439
the Staff aren’t exactly crafty, this could
actually work. However, if your disguise is

00:07:07.439 --> 00:07:11.870
good enough to fool other members of the staff
then there’s a good chance that other survivors

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:17.439
living in 3008 might think you are actually
a member of the Staff running around at night,

00:07:17.439 --> 00:07:22.729
and you may end up taking a Vörda chef’s
knife to the face. $9.99 in the kitchen section.

00:07:22.729 --> 00:07:26.570
Random User said, “As soon as night comes
I’d simply lock myself in the nearest bathroom

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:30.590
with some furniture, and cry. Then when the
morning comes I’ll get my daily rations

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.150
and the cycle repeats-”

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:36.439
Not a bad idea. We personally use this method
in our own lives every single day, and we’re

00:07:36.439 --> 00:07:43.569
not even trapped in the infinite Ikea.
Sam Yates said, “I’d build some sort of

00:07:43.569 --> 00:07:48.120
fortress out of big thick rugs… The staff
could attack and break a base made of wood…

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:51.370
but can you easily punch your way through
a rug? I dunno…”

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:55.939
Strangely, there’s been very little research
into that area, Sam. Perhaps rugs are the

00:07:55.939 --> 00:08:00.520
ultimate recipe for fortress structural integrity.
Maybe all those kings and queens and dukes

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:05.320
and counts were wrong, and stone castles weren’t
the answer, it was rugs the whole time. The

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:09.930
problem is, if you’re wrong and the Staff
gets in, it’ll be the last mistake you ever

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.979
made, as you die on a pile of Langsted and
Stangerum rugs.

00:08:13.979 --> 00:08:17.979
Pope Koolaid said, “I’d do what any middle
class American would do in that situation,

00:08:17.979 --> 00:08:18.979
get my gun.”

00:08:18.979 --> 00:08:23.819
Sorry to tell you, Holy Father, but they don’t
sell guns in Ikea. Unless you like taking

00:08:23.819 --> 00:08:28.509
your gun to Ikea with you all the time, just
in case one of those shady Överskådlig fridges

00:08:28.509 --> 00:08:29.699
tries something.

00:08:29.699 --> 00:08:33.390
Shrek’s Cousin said, “Easy, just file
a lawsuit saying that one of the employees

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:34.560
injured you.”

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:40.570
This might get you a pretty hefty cash settlement
from Ikea...if you ever escape, and the SCP

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:44.960
Foundation doesn't get you with amnestics
first. The Staff unfortunately, seem to have

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.710
less respect for the rule of law.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:53.890
Moocow4u2 said, “Talk about SCP-2521 and
be instantly removed from the store.”

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:58.330
This would be a method to escape, yes, but
we can’t promise you’d like where it takes

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.060
you any more than SCP-3008.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:04.260
Tiny Sarv said, “I would tell the Staff
that they should let me see their manager

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:07.440
for the poor customer service, and if I die,
so be it.”

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:14.930
Ah, the little-known SCP-3008-3, also known
as… the Karen. The one entity found within

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:20.260
SCP-3008 that is perhaps even more terrifying
than the Staff. You can definitely try this

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:23.889
technique, but we can’t promise it will
get the results you want. There doesn’t

00:09:23.889 --> 00:09:27.640
seem to be an entity above the Staff that
is controlling them, or even managing their

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:32.890
schedules and days off like Demon Dan’s
unseen supervisor. But if there was, it would

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:37.630
likely be something even more terrifying than
the staff, and would probably think that the

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:42.700
staff is doing an a-okay job and if you don’t
like it you can take your business elsewhere.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.870
Dawawa said, “I’d simply die.”

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:49.320
Hey, we appreciate your honesty, at least.
But we think it’s generally better to hold

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:55.450
onto hope, try your best to survive and perhaps
even escape this terrifying anomalous situation.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:59.300
After all, you’re only truly out when you
count yourself out.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:05.070
P&amp;Qcowboy Channel said, “I would start to
worship the staff. And even give them sacrifices.”

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:10.850
This is definitely a creative solution, but
not one that we actually think would solve

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:15.580
anything. After all, The Staff aren’t actually
sentient beings, they seem to act on pure

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:20.850
instinct, attacking any interlopers within
the store at night. So no amount of sacrifices

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:25.210
will ever truly appease them. You’re better
off teaming up with other humans and fighting

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:26.650
for survival.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:30.150
Grace Ng said, “I’ll eat the monsters,
they look delicious.”

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:35.600
Well, thank you for sharing, Grace. And as
for the rest of you, if you ever find yourself

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:40.310
inside the infinite Ikea, and you happen to
see Grace prowling the showroom near you,

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:45.030
then perhaps keep your distance - especially
if she looks hungry. If she’s willing to

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:48.520
eat the Staff, who knows what else she’s
capable of?

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:52.160
Fortnite Stuff said, “I would survive in
a weird way, I would die, then I would be

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.160
out.”

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:57.700
While we suppose you would technically be
out of the infinite Ikea in a grim existential

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:02.700
sense, we think you may have misunderstood
the meaning of “Survive” there. But don’t

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.740
worry, you’ll be able to learn about all
that and more from our new sister channel,

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:10.450
“Words: Explained.”
Okay, I made that up. Sorry.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:16.370
MrMisterDerp said, “As someone who has been
in several ikeas, NEVER USE THE MENS ROOM!!!”

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:22.130
We’re so sorry. We can only imagine the
horrific things you’ve seen, it’d probably

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.220
make 682 shudder in fear.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:28.480
Kiryu-Chan said, “I would build a community
inside and make myself the leader, make people

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:32.540
fight and find food on my behalf! Nothing
is better than being lazy and having people

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.640
at your command.”

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:38.790
While all of the strange communities within
SCP-3008 do require a leader, if you try to

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:43.580
install yourself as some kind of flat-pack
dictator, chances are you’re going to get

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:48.020
overthrown during a revolution and exiled.
At which point, you’ll probably be killed

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:53.790
by the Staff. The message? Be nice to people.
Kindness costs nothing, after all, and if

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:57.180
you’re going to be trapped in an Ikea with
a bunch of strangers for potentially years

00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:01.050
on end, you’re going to want them to actually
like you.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:06.450
Toxic Dynamix said, “I would just watch
"The Infographic show's" video "You vs SCP-3008"

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.740
and do what they say.”

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:12.130
Yes, that’s an excellent video, containing
everything you need to know about surviving

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:17.110
your time in SCP-3008. I think we should all
watch it, and then subscribe to the Infographics

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:20.850
Show for more great videos every day, and
of course, ring the bell to turn on notifications.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:24.040
That’s the best idea we’ve heard all day.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:28.950
And there we have it, folks! Thanks to everyone
for sending in their thoughts and ideas. If

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:32.620
you want to be involved in the next one, keep
an eye on our community posts for the next

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:38.410
opportunity for you to throw in your two SCP
cents! And in the meantime, maybe do your

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.790
furniture shopping online...

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:46.300
Now check out “SCP-3008 - Trapped in IKEA”
and “SCP-087 - The Stairwell” for more

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:48.590
SCPs you’ll really want to get out of!

